## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of end-to-end testing in a complex, multi-region, event-sourced delivery application. It checks whether the candidate can design tests that cover data isolation, cross-region convergence, failure handling, and compliance scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- Event-sourced E2E flows with Kafka domain topics and region-specific read models
- Cross-region consistency and latency budget validation
- Multi-tenant data isolation and DSAR (Data Subject Access Request) compliance
- Fault injection including regional outages and retry mechanisms
- Observability integration and deterministic seed data

## Code Example
```javascript
// Seed deterministic test data and publish events to Kafka; verify read-model convergence
const seedOrder = { id: 'ORD-123', tenantId: 'tenant-acme', region: 'us-east' };

await kafka.publish('orders.us-east', { 
  eventType: 'OrderPlaced', 
  payload: seedOrder, 
  timestamp: '2026-01-15T10:00:00Z' 
});

await kafka.publish('drivers.us-east', {
  eventType: 'DriverAssigned',
  payload: { orderId: 'ORD-123', driverId: 'DRV-456' }
});

// Verify real-time WebSocket delivery to clients
const wsUpdate = await waitForWebSocketMessage('rider-client', 'ETAUpdated');
expect(wsUpdate.payload.eta).toBeWithinSLA();

// Validate cross-region read-model convergence
const readModel = await readModelClient.query('us-west', 'orders', { id: 'ORD-123' });
expect(readModel.status).toEqual('confirmed');
expect(readModel.convergenceTime).toBeLessThan(SLA_THRESHOLD_MS);

// Verify tenant isolation
const crossTenantResult = await readModelClient.query('us-east', 'orders', { 
  id: 'ORD-123', 
  tenantId: 'tenant-foreign' 
});
expect(crossTenantResult.accessDenied).toBe(true);

// DSAR deletion verification
await dsarService.requestDeletion('customer-789');
await waitForEventProcessing();
const piiCheck = await readModelClient.scanAllRegions('customer-789');
expect(piiCheck.found).toBe(false);

// Region failover test
await regionOutageSimulator.failover('us-east', 'us-west');
const failoverState = await readModelClient.getState('us-west', 'ORD-123');
expect(failoverState.reconstructed).toBe(true);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a beginner-friendly E2E scenario involving asynchronous background work, multiple data stores, and end-to-end verification of UI and backend state.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end vs component tests
- Asynchronous processing and polling
- Test data seeding and isolation
- Mocking external services with determinism
- Retry and failure handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test sketch (Playwright/Cypress style)
// Seed user/feed
seedUser({ id: 'u1' });
// Upload
uploadImage('/path/photo.jpg');
// Mock storage to return fixed URLs
mockStorageUrls({ original: 'https://storage/img/orig.jpg', s1: 'https://storage/img/s1.jpg', s2: 'https://storage/img/s2.jpg', s3: 'https://storage/img/s3.jpg' });
// Poll for processing completion
waitForProcessing('image-upload-u1', 60000);
// Verify feed shows three sizes
verifyFeedItemHasSizes(['orig','s1','s2','s3']);
// Verify search index entry
verifyIndexEntry({ id: 'img-u1', urls: ['orig','s1','s2','s3'] });
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle flaky network conditions during the image upload in this test?
- How would you extend this to verify eventual consistency if the index updates survive a restart?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests RBAC in a realistic multi-tenant admin UI with progressive permission changes, ensuring isolation and correct UI cues.

## Key Concepts
- RBAC policies per-tenant
- Test data seeding and isolation
- UI visibility vs. API enforcement
- Role upgrade propagation without relogin

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example sketch
test('RBAC per-tenant role upgrade', async ({ page }) => {
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'viewer');
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/dashboard/);
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeHidden();
  await upgradeRole(page, 'TenantA', 'u1', 'editor');
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('#user-management')).toBeVisible();
  await loginAsTenantUser(page, 'TenantB', 'u2', 'viewer');
  await expect(page.locator('#tenant-data')).toHaveText(/TenantA/).toBeHidden();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle flaky network affecting role-change propagation? 
- What assertions would you add to guard against stale caches after role changes?

