## Why This Is Asked
Tests for per-user feature flags are common in SaaS apps. This question checks the ability to seed data, perform API-driven state changes, and verify UI behavior across login and page reloads in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Per-user feature flags and API seed/reset
- End-to-end UI verification of dynamic layouts
- Test isolation and deterministic CI runs

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example using Playwright-like syntax (pseudocode)
// seedUser(), setFlag(), login() are helper utilities
test('compact dashboard toggling', async ({ page, request }) => {
  const { userId, email, password } = await seedUser(request);
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', true);
  await login(page, email, password);
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-compact')).toBeVisible();
  await setFlag(request, userId, 'CompactDashboard', false);
  await page.reload();
  await expect(page.locator('.dashboard-full')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you guard against flaky UI assertions caused by caching?
- How would you extend the test to cover multiple user segments (roles/regions) and parallel execution?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design end-to-end checks for multi-tenant isolation, safe canary rollouts, per-tenant quotas, and rollback safety, all under realistic load patterns and with observability built in.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant data isolation and namespaces
- Canary feature flag rollout and traffic shaping
- Per-tenant quotas and burst load handling
- Data leakage prevention across tenants
- Rollback safety and path reversions
- Observability: traces, metrics, logs, alerting

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: toggle canary flag for a tenant and verify routing change
async function testCanaryTenant(tenantId){
  await api.setFeatureFlag({tenantId, flag: 'NEW_SEARCH', value: true, rollout: 0.2});
  const traces = await tracing.collect(tenantId);
  const path = traces.find(t => t.name === 'searchBackend');
  assert(path.usedNewBackend === true);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate rollback safety under observed latency spikes?
- What metrics and alerting thresholds would you define for this rollout?

